<div class="blurb" id="dependencies-section" role="region" aria-labelledby="dependencies-heading">
  <div class="header">
    <h2 id="dependencies-heading">Technical Details / Dependencies</h2>
  </div>
  <div class="body">
    <h3>Dependencies</h3>
    <ul>
      <li>Python 3.9 – 3.12</li>
      <li>OpenCV 4.9.0 (Qt backend by default; GTK needed for some legacy demos)</li>
      <li>cvzone (provides hand tracking and gesture utilities via MediaPipe)</li>
      <li>NumPy</li>
      <li>PyOpenGL (optional, for GPU-based rendering in OpenGL demos)</li>
      <li>pyvirtualcam (for virtual camera output; compatible with OBS and Zoom)</li>
    </ul>
    <p>
      Note: MediaPipe is only supported by the Python versions listed above; cvzone depends on MediaPipe for gesture and face detection.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
